                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Greenville-Spartanburg SC",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 23 at 1:15AM EDT until September 23 at 5:45AM EDT by NWS Greenville-Spartanburg SC",
                "description": "At 115 AM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 2.5 and 4 inches of rain have\nfallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLake Lure, Chimney Rock Village, Chimney Rock State Park, Bat Cave\nand Gerton.\n\nFlood stage is currently 7.43 feet at the Rocky Broad River near Bat\nCave. Homes and campgrounds near the river gage will begin to flood\nif the river gets above 7.5 feet.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
