                "senderName": "NWS Wakefield VA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 22 at 11:48PM EDT until September 23 at 3:00AM EDT by NWS Wakefield VA",
                "description": "FFWAKQ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Wakefield has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCumberland County in central Virginia...\nPowhatan County in central Virginia...\n\n* Until 300 AM EDT.\n\n* At 1148 PM EDT, gauge reports indicated heavy rain falling across\nthe warned area. Up to 3 inches of rain has fallen in the past two\nhours. The expected rainfall rate is 2 inches in 1 hour and 30\nminutes. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Gauges reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPowhatan, Cumberland, Tobaccoville, Ballsville, Sunnyside,\nTrenholm, Macon, Guinea Mills, Clinton, Hatchers, Belona, Oak\nForest, Ashby, Whiteville, Grays Siding, Lake Powhatan, Tamworth,\nProvost and Rock Castle.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nPlease report flooding by calling 757-899-2415, posting to the NWS\nWakefield Facebook page, or using X @NWSWAKEFIELDVA.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
